Patient Name: William Harris
DOB: 1965-07-30
MRN: 55667788
Admission Date: 2026-05-02
Discharge Date: 2026-05-07
Primary Diagnosis: Acute ischemic stroke (left MCA territory)
Hospital Course Summary:
- Presented with acute right-sided weakness and aphasia; received IV tPA within window and monitored in neuro ICU.
- MRI confirmed left MCA infarct; speech and physical therapy engaged early with measurable improvement.
- Blood pressure and glucose controlled; initiated secondary prevention measures.
Medications at Discharge:
- Aspirin 81 mg PO daily
- Atorvastatin 40 mg PO nightly
- Antihypertensive regimen as per discharge instructions
- Home anticoagulation not started pending stroke team decision (see notes)
Follow-up:
- Neurology clinic in 1 week.
- Outpatient PT/OT and speech therapy referrals arranged.
Home Instructions:
- Fall precautions; assistive devices as recommended by therapists.
- Resume driving and heavy machinery only after clearance from neurology.
Return Precautions / Red Flags:
- New or worsening weakness, new speech changes, sudden severe headache, or loss of consciousness -> seek emergency care immediately.
Allergies: NKDA
Discharge Disposition: Home with outpatient therapy services
Discharge Summary Prepared By: Dr. K. O'Neil
